message: "If you use this software, please cite the software release and the associated paper."

title: "Observability of Velocity Derivatives from Kinetic Populations in the Lattice Boltzmann Method"
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Cuoci"
    given-names: "Alberto"

version: "1.0.0"

date-released: "2026-08-23"

license: "MIT"

repository-code: "https://github.com/acuoci/lbm_ce2_validation"

url: "https://github.com/acuoci/lbm_ce2_validation"

abstract: >
  Python implementation and reproducibility material for the numerical
  validation of kinetic derivative observability in D2Q9, D3Q19, and
  D3Q27 lattice Boltzmann models. The repository contains the numerical
  experiments supporting the associated Physics of Fluids manuscript,
  including finite-wavenumber D2Q9 shear-mode validation,
  three-dimensional D3Q19/D3Q27 CE2 population-response calculations,
  and a weakly nonlinear Taylor-Green cross-check.

keywords:
  - Lattice Boltzmann Method
  - LBM
  - kinetic populations
  - Chapman-Enskog expansion
  - observability
  - D2Q9
  - D3Q19
  - D3Q27
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - reproducibility

